# HR Analytics Dashboard – Executive Summary

## 1. Project Overview

The **HR Analytics Dashboard** is an interactive dashboard developed in **Microsoft Excel** to transform raw employee data into meaningful business insights. It provides HR professionals with a centralized view of key workforce metrics, enabling faster and more informed decision-making through interactive charts, Pivot Tables, and slicers.

---

## 2. Business Problem

Organizations often manage HR data across multiple spreadsheets, making it difficult to analyze employee information efficiently. Manual reporting is time-consuming, error-prone, and limits visibility into workforce trends such as employee demographics, salary distribution, skills, leave records, and employment types.

---

## 3. Proposed Solution

To address these challenges, an interactive HR dashboard was created using **Microsoft Excel**. The dashboard consolidates HR data into a single, user-friendly interface, allowing users to filter, analyze, and visualize workforce information in real time, reducing manual effort and improving reporting efficiency.

---

## 4. Project Objectives

* Build an interactive HR Analytics Dashboard using Microsoft Excel.
* Analyze employee demographics, employment types, and gender distribution.
* Monitor employee skills, work locations, and leave records.
* Compare salary distribution across job categories.
* Support HR professionals with data-driven decision-making.

---

## 5. Dashboard Components

* **Employment Type Analysis** – Displays Full-Time, Part-Time, and Contract employees.
* **Age & Gender Analysis** – Analyzes workforce demographics by age group and gender.
* **Skills Analysis** – Visualizes employee skills and identifies workforce competencies.
* **Work Location Analysis** – Compares employees across Branch Office, Head Office, and Remote locations.
* **Employee Leave Analysis** – Tracks leave records to support workforce planning.
* **Salary Analysis** – Compares salaries across different job roles.
* **Gender Distribution** – Shows workforce diversity using gender-based analysis.

---

## 6. Key Insights

* Full-Time employees make up the largest share of the workforce.
* Most employees fall within the 26–45 years age group.
* Communication, Design, and Management are the most common skills.
* Branch Offices have the highest employee count.
* Managers receive the highest average salaries.
* Leave analysis supports effective workforce planning.
* Gender distribution provides insights into organizational diversity.

---

## 7. Business Impact

* Reduced manual HR reporting.
* Improved reporting accuracy and efficiency.
* Enabled faster, data-driven HR decisions.
* Enhanced workforce planning and resource allocation.
* Simplified HR performance monitoring through interactive visualizations.

